data medium_structure_grammar_classifier_note: String = "no-smuggled-programs wall (HALF B): this lens is a GRAMMAR CLASSIFIER over substrate string literals, replacing the marker heuristic (medium_syntax_markers deleted). The seed (medium_structure_literal_parts_facts, ruling R1b grammar/language-ignorant) enumerates RawLine.text / Heredoc.body field-expression PARTS as neutral [Const|Hole]; this lens applies the TYPE-STRUCTURAL language gate and runs bash_composition_recognizer. A composition of a modeled language = typed/located/COUNTED Violation; an atom = Clean; the undecidable residue = counted AmbiguousParse (DecodeFidelity). The gate SUPERSEDES the coarse path-exemption: no RawLine/Heredoc CONSTRUCTION exists in any path-exempt dir, so the path-exemption exempts zero classified sites (kept as harmless mostly-dead, dissolves with the marker era). ConstructionJustification = WallAfterGrounding (marker heuristic -> grammar classifier); the genuine-Unknown AmbiguousParse residue is RatchetForever."

data medium_structure_type_structural_gate_note: String = "The language-decision gate is the ShellStmt coproduct (dag/extdeps/languages/bash/program.dag): every variant is MODELED structure EXCEPT the two String-carrying smuggling vectors RawLine{text} and Heredoc{body}. RawLine.text is definitionally bash. Heredoc.body language depends on the target, but the emit (program.dag) hardwires cat > path (the body is WRITTEN TO A FILE as data, never piped to an interpreter), so the type cannot name a language -> AmbiguousParse{NoLanguageDecision} interim (UNRESOLVED-language framing: a heredoc writing a bash script then exec IS smuggled but the model cannot see the deferred exec; a target-resolution follow-up can reclassify bash-target heredoc to Violation, so counted Ambiguous rows stay a LIVE ledger, not a permanent silent gap)."

data medium_bash_sink_targets: List<String> = ["RawLine.text", "Heredoc.body"]

type RawLiteralPart {
  is_hole: Bool
  text: String
}

type RawLiteralPartsFact {
  path: String
  constructor: String
  field: String
  parts: List<RawLiteralPart>
}

data empty_skeleton_parts: List<SkeletonPart> = []

fn part_to_skeleton(p: RawLiteralPart) -> SkeletonPart {
  if p.is_hole {
    HolePart
  } else {
    ConstPart { text: p.text }
  }
}

fn parts_to_skeleton(parts: List<RawLiteralPart>) -> LiteralSkeleton {
  LiteralSkeleton {
    parts: fold_list(
      xs: parts,
      empty: empty_skeleton_parts,
      cons: fn(acc, p) { list_snoc_item(xs: acc, item: part_to_skeleton(p: p)) }
    )
  }
}

fn constructor_field_matches(fact: RawLiteralPartsFact, ctor: String, field: String) -> Bool {
  (fact.constructor == ctor) && (fact.field == field)
}

fn classify_raw_literal_fact(fact: RawLiteralPartsFact) -> BashCompositionDisposition {
  if constructor_field_matches(fact: fact, ctor: "RawLine", field: "text") {
    classify_bash_skeleton(sk: parts_to_skeleton(parts: fact.parts))
  } else {
    AmbiguousParse { cause: NoLanguageDecision }
  }
}

data medium_scope_note: String = "The live scan scope is the PRODUCTION SUBSTRATE (std/extdeps/compiler/tools/gunbc/workflow/lens), which EXCLUDES test/claim. This is an EXPLICIT, documented scope (NOT a silent narrowing): a test that constructs RawLine to exercise the bash fold (bash_command_fold_test.dag builds RawLine as fold INPUT, incl. a 2-line RawLine) legitimately builds the escape hatch, and flagging a TEST of the escape hatch is a category error. The wall's threat model is accidental hand-splicing in the substrate. Fixtures (planted/perturb) are passed as explicit perturb roots, so they are unaffected by this default scope."

